  Every page of z-privacy.com, and nothing else.

  Every address, each one the address its own page calls canonical, each
  with the language versions that page itself names. It was nine until the
  three terms pages of 097, twelve until the three guide pages of 100, and
  fifteen until the three download pages of 103 — a number written in a
  comment is a number nobody measures, so the guard counts the tree and this
  line is only a reader’s note. Nothing is listed here
  that a reader cannot reach from the site, and nothing the site serves is
  left out: scripts/check_sitemap.py walks this list against the tree in
  both directions, so a page added later and forgotten here goes red before
  it is ever published.

  The owner’s private preview folder is deliberately absent. A sitemap is a
  public invitation, and keeping something out of the index is the server’s
  work, not a line in a file that names it.
-->
